## ✅ Work DONE (Backend)

### 1. [overpass.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/utils/overpass.ts) — `NEW`
- Builds Overpass QL queries to fetch `village`, `hamlet`, `locality` nodes from OpenStreetMap
- Parses raw Overpass JSON into `{ name, latitude, longitude }` array
- Prefers Hindi name (`name_hi`) if available
- Computes bounding box from route coordinates with 5km padding
- **Multi-endpoint fallback**: tries 3 Overpass mirrors (overpass-api.de → kumi.systems → mail.ru)
- Uses `node-fetch` (not native fetch) with proper `Accept: application/json` header
- 70-second timeout with `AbortController`

### 2. [villageFilter.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/utils/villageFilter.ts) — `NEW`
- Pure distance-filtering function: keeps villages within `maxDistanceKm` of route polyline
- Uses existing `distanceToPolylineKm()` from `geoUtils.ts` (Cartesian projection)
- Default threshold: **5 km** (configurable)
- Sorted by distance ascending (nearest first)
- Completely isolated from ETA/live-distance logic

### 3. [routeVillages.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/api/routeVillages.ts) — `NEW`
- Express router with 2 endpoints:
  - `GET /:routeId/villages?maxDistanceKm=5` — returns filtered villages
  - `POST /:routeId/villages/refresh` — forces Overpass re-fetch
- **File-based cache** at `src/db/village_cache/<routeId>.json`
- 7-day TTL; serves stale cache as fallback if Overpass is unreachable
- Re-filters from cache on custom `maxDistanceKm` requests

